ge. In the UI: right-click node 121 → Mode → Always (or its bypass toggle).\n\nRaise the \"f2k_consis\" LoRA strength (id 122, currently 0.3). A LoRA named \"consis\" is almost certainly there specifically for identity/character consistency — try 0.5–0.8 and see how it looks before pushing further.\n\nRaise CFG in the CFGGuider node (id 106, currently 1.0). At CFG=1 the negative conditioning has essentially zero effect, so there's nothing pulling the result away from generic/hallucinated features. Try 2.0–3.5 in small steps — too high causes oversaturation/artifacts.\n\nNudge the \"klein_snofs_v1_4\" LoRA strength (currently 1.0) up to 1.1–1.3. This is presumably the subject-specific LoRA itself. Push cautiously — overshooting causes waxy skin/warped features.\n\nIncrease the reference image resolution feeding the conditioning: ImageScaleToTotalPixels (id 119) is set to 2 megapixels — bumping to 3–4 (VRAM permitting) gives the reference latent more facial detail to draw identity from.\n\nAdd a few more sampling steps in Flux2Scheduler (currently 25) — try 30–40, especially if you raise CFG, since higher CFG needs more steps to converge cleanly."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":123,"type":"Image Comparer (rgthree)","pos":[783.6146487801191,1659.5922049340159],"size":[922.8122804454864,1241.5401022183141],"flags":{},"order":23,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"dir":3,"name":"image_a","type":"IMAGE","link":210},{"dir":3,"name":"image_b","type":"IMAGE","link":211}],"outputs":[{"dir":4,"name":"images","shape":3,"type":"IMAGE","links":null}],"properties":{"comparer_mode":"Slide","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":[[{"name":"A","selected":true,"url":"/api/view?filename=rgthree.compare._temp_ozuko_00037_.png&type=temp&subfolder=&rand=0.5968180332333225"},{"name":"B","selected":true,"url":"/api/view?filename=rgthree.compare._temp_ozuko_00038_.png&type=temp&subfolder=&rand=0.13559432581911313"}]]},{"id":76,"ty